# Cloudflare adds a matching rule's headers to what is already there; it does
# not replace them. The first version of this file assumed the opposite — a
# broad "/*" default followed by narrower exceptions — and the deploy check
# printed what that actually produced:
#
#   page   cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
#   bundle cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000, immutable
#
# Two max-age values on one header, and a client is free to honour either. The
# year-long cache on content-hashed files was the whole point of that rule, and
# it had been quietly cancelled by the rule above it.
#
# So no overlapping rules here, and no broad default: pages carry Cloudflare's
# own default for static assets, which is the must-revalidate line above and is
# exactly what is wanted. The deploy asserts both — that pages still revalidate
# and that no asset comes back with a contradictory header — because that is a
# property of Cloudflare's behaviour rather than of anything in this repo, and
# it is the kind of thing that changes without telling you.
#
# The stake is higher here than the usual cache tuning: asset filenames are
# content-hashed and each deploy replaces the whole set, so a page held stale
# anywhere between the origin and the reader asks for files that no longer
# exist. Those 404 into the SPA fallback, which answers with HTML, and the
# browser then refuses both the stylesheet and the module — leaving the
# prerendered text unstyled, which is the failure being chased on a locked-down
# laptop.

# Hashed filenames never change contents, so they can be cached forever.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The calendar is rewritten twice a week; a short TTL means a refresh shows up
# quickly without hammering the origin.
/data/releases.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

# The whole point of this page is to report what the network in front of it is
# doing. A cached copy of it would report on a different day's network.
/diag/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
